# phase8_statutory.powl — Phase 8: Statutory Merger Share Exchange & DGCL §251 Authorization
#
# Contract: E-M08 lane (MX5 dispatch, 2026-10-11) — 6-place/5-transition spine
#   PlanIngest → ContinuityGate → ShareExchange → DGCLAuthorize → CertIssue.
# Grammar: src/conformance/loader.rs:11-31; PowlModel::from_powl_str
# (loader.rs:638); MAX_POWL_NODES = 64 (loader.rs:47). Lowering/session laws:
# ConformanceSession (session.rs), linear lowering = each DFS atom once
# (xor branches flatten in the model-derived golden — phase5 precedent).
#
# Embedded invariants as structure (E-M08's four laws):
# - ORDERING / NO-BYPASS: the five spine transitions sit in one strict
#   `sequence`; no transition is reachable out of order and no spine transition
#   is bypassable (linear lowering tid = atom index, tick = prev+1 carries the
#   order — a dropped spine atom faults `Skipped` at its step).
# - EXACT SHARE-COUNT EQUALITY (zero over-issuance, conservation loop): the
#   exchange runs as a bounded loop; every `share_exchange` iteration carries
#   exchanged_shares == outstanding_shares in its OCEL attributes. The
#   structural-equality check itself is the invariants-lane court (attributes
#   are UNSUPPORTED at the packed tier), not a net node — the loop bound
#   (max 12) keeps the conservation walk finite.
# - ONE-SHOT CERTIFICATE: `cert_issue` appears exactly once, outside the loop,
#   terminal on its xor branch — a second issuance is structurally unreachable
#   (a repeated cert_issue faults `Skipped`, the phase5 loop-repetition law).
# - FAIL-CLOSED REFUSAL ABSORPTION: DGCL refusal is not a silent no-fire —
#   `refusal_absorb` is a declared terminal branch of the post-authorization
#   xor that carries the seeded refusal reason (reason=dgcl-subsidiary-vote-
#   failed, reason=appraisal-demand-open) as replay events and terminates the
#   case without a certificate. The xor keeps the two outcomes mutually
#   exclusive in the graph; the linear lowering walks both branches in the
#   model-derived golden (phase5 precedent — act_admitted + act_refused).
#
# Case-id convention (E-M09 master-trace namespacing): phase-local case ids are
# namespaced `p8-<case>` (e.g. p8-statutory-1).
#
# OCEL fixture note: the phase-8 fixtures (conformance/phase8_statutory*.ocel.json)
# use the in-crate `ocel:*` map projection accepted by import_ocel_json
# (import_json.rs:67-77) — ocel:version "2.0", ocel:events as a map keyed by
# event id, ocel:timestamp u64 ns, ocel:activity, ocel:caseId.
#
# Node budget: 10 / 64 (MAX_POWL_NODES, loader.rs:47).

activity plan_ingest     = merger.plan_filing            # t_plan_ingest (1)     -> p_plan_ingested
activity continuity_gate = merger.continuity_check       # t_continuity_gate (2) -> p_continuity_gated
activity share_exchange  = merger.share_exchange         # t_share_exchange (3)  -> p_exchanged (conservation loop, zero over-issuance)
activity dgcl_authorize  = merger.dgcl_251_authorize     # t_dgcl_authorize (4)  -> p_authorized
activity cert_issue      = merger.certificate_issue      # t_cert_issue (5)      -> p_certified (one-shot)
activity refusal_absorb  = merger.dgcl_refusal_absorb    #                       -> p_refused (fail-closed terminal, no certificate)

sequence {
  plan_ingest                                               # spine 1/5: plan of merger filing (no bypass)
  continuity_gate                                           # spine 2/5: continuity of shareholders/directors
  loop { share_exchange } redo { silent } max 12            # spine 3/5: conservation loop — issued == outstanding
  dgcl_authorize                                            # spine 4/5: DGCL §251 board + shareholder authorization
  xor {                                                     # one-shot certificate vs fail-closed refusal absorption
    cert_issue                                              # spine 5/5: exactly one certificate, ever
    refusal_absorb                                          # refusal reasons ride the event; terminal, no cert
  }
}
